    "reason": "evidence sufficient (proxy gate verdict; the open aspects need proposals): The cited item [ev-4beb2699f685] is only a bare metric name. However, the section introduction [ev-1f419676f177] explains what the list means. It says these metrics, which started with `cortex_`, are renamed in this release to start with `loki_`, because the default `metrics_namespace` is now `loki`. It also says operators can keep the old prefix by setting `metrics_namespace` to `cortex`, a setting that is deprecated and will be removed in the next minor release. That is enough to write the assertion: the subject is the metric `cortex_prometheus_notifications_latency_seconds`; the change is a rename to `loki_prometheus_notifications_latency_seconds`; environments that have not set `metrics_namespace: cortex` are exposed; and if they do nothing, the metric is no longer published under its old name.",
